{"id":"2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new","date":"2026-10-18","topic":"health","region":"americas","headline":"Stanford scientists build new microscope for living cells","source":{"name":"ScienceDaily","url":"https://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2026/10/261015073231.htm"},"accent":"us","tiers":{"t1":{"sentences":[{"text":"Stanford school people made a new glass system.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t1-0.m4a","dur":3.23,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t1-0.m4a","durJa":4.92,"times":[0.0,0.4,0.88,1.34,1.68,1.88,2.12,2.46]},{"text":"This system shows small parts move inside live forms.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t1-1.m4a","dur":4.0,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t1-1.m4a","durJa":5.45,"times":[0.0,0.14,0.46,0.72,1.14,1.68,2.08,2.5,3.14]},{"text":"The team did not put color on the parts.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t1-2.m4a","dur":2.18,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t1-2.m4a","durJa":2.92,"times":[0.0,0.12,0.34,0.54,0.76,1.0,1.28,1.5,1.58]},{"text":"The new machine helps people study health and body work.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t1-3.m4a","dur":3.57,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t1-3.m4a","durJa":6.19,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.24,0.5,0.92,1.2,1.62,2.0,2.32,2.58]}],"bands":{"core1000":94,"core1800":3,"ngsl":0,"tsl":0,"nawl":0,"beyond":3}},"t2":{"sentences":[{"text":"Stanford researchers built a new system to view live cells.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t2-0.m4a","dur":4.82,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t2-0.m4a","durJa":7.1,"times":[0.0,0.46,1.32,1.76,2.02,2.28,2.72,3.14,3.4,3.88]},{"text":"The technology reveals small structures moving inside living cells clearly.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t2-1.m4a","dur":5.56,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t2-1.m4a","durJa":5.76,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.5,1.06,1.68,2.42,3.0,3.52,4.2,4.5]},{"text":"Scientists did not use glowing markers for the views.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t2-2.m4a","dur":3.54,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t2-2.m4a","durJa":4.09,"times":[0.0,0.32,0.82,1.12,1.48,1.86,2.34,2.82,2.94]},{"text":"This device will help researchers study health and various diseases.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t2-3.m4a","dur":4.49,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t2-3.m4a","durJa":5.32,"times":[0.0,0.16,0.44,0.76,1.02,1.42,2.1,2.54,3.06,3.48]},{"text":"The new technology protects cells from harm during long tests.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t2-4.m4a","dur":4.6,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t2-4.m4a","durJa":5.26,"times":[0.0,0.12,0.32,0.84,1.38,2.06,2.4,2.68,3.08,3.38]}],"bands":{"core1000":82,"core1800":10,"ngsl":2,"tsl":0,"nawl":2,"beyond":4}},"t3":{"sentences":[{"text":"Researchers at Stanford University have developed an advanced system for living cells.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t3-0.m4a","dur":5.45,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t3-0.m4a","durJa":6.36,"times":[0.0,0.48,0.92,1.2,2.14,2.44,2.76,3.12,3.4,3.92,4.32,4.64]},{"text":"The instrument shows small internal structures moving and interacting in real time.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t3-1.m4a","dur":5.41,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t3-1.m4a","durJa":6.31,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.42,0.82,1.24,1.8,2.5,3.18,3.56,4.06,4.5,4.74]},{"text":"Scientists can observe cell activity clearly without using glowing labels.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t3-2.m4a","dur":4.66,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t3-2.m4a","durJa":6.11,"times":[0.0,0.3,0.78,1.0,1.4,1.88,2.36,2.86,3.46,3.78]},{"text":"This technology helps experts study how cells respond to medicines and health issues.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t3-3.m4a","dur":4.93,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t3-3.m4a","durJa":6.53,"times":[0.0,0.14,0.54,0.94,1.46,1.86,2.18,2.44,2.96,3.22,3.6,4.02,4.24]},{"text":"The system avoids problems like fading signals and changes in cell behavior.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t3-4.m4a","dur":4.34,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t3-4.m4a","durJa":5.56,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.3,0.6,1.1,1.44,1.82,2.44,2.76,3.14,3.44,3.64]},{"text":"Lower light exposure protects living biological systems from potential harm.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t3-5.m4a","dur":4.86,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t3-5.m4a","durJa":6.51,"times":[0.0,0.3,0.54,0.94,1.54,2.02,2.5,3.16,3.5,3.86]}],"bands":{"core1000":77,"core1800":15,"ngsl":6,"tsl":0,"nawl":1,"beyond":1}},"t4":{"sentences":[{"text":"A novel imaging system developed at Stanford University reveals the inner workings of living cells.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t4-0.m4a","dur":6.89,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t4-0.m4a","durJa":8.03,"times":[0.0,0.16,0.46,0.98,1.54,1.96,2.3,2.68,3.6,4.14,4.54,4.86,5.38,5.76,6.08]},{"text":"By combining two advanced techniques, the microscope achieves high resolution without artificial tags.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t4-1.m4a","dur":6.79,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t4-1.m4a","durJa":7.5,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.5,0.88,1.24,2.56,2.72,2.98,3.66,4.0,4.68,5.22,5.8]},{"text":"Researchers can monitor multiple cell components simultaneously without relying on special markers.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t4-2.m4a","dur":6.4,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t4-2.m4a","durJa":7.03,"times":[0.0,0.3,0.68,1.04,1.62,1.98,2.58,3.02,4.4,4.84,5.16,5.5]},{"text":"Traditional methods often alter cell behavior or fade during extended observation periods.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t4-3.m4a","dur":5.69,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t4-3.m4a","durJa":7.49,"times":[0.0,0.32,0.8,1.3,1.7,2.1,2.44,3.02,3.38,3.8,4.28,4.6]},{"text":"The new technology requires less illumination power, thereby reducing the risk of damage.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t4-4.m4a","dur":5.7,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t4-4.m4a","durJa":6.96,"times":[0.0,0.12,0.3,0.76,1.16,1.94,2.5,3.5,3.78,4.3,4.66,4.94,5.06]},{"text":"Scientists believe this breakthrough will advance research in health and various conditions.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t4-5.m4a","dur":5.43,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t4-5.m4a","durJa":7.84,"times":[0.0,0.36,0.86,1.3,1.74,2.22,2.54,3.16,3.52,3.82,4.14,4.5]},{"text":"The team emphasizes that the system complements existing methods rather than replacing them.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t4-6.m4a","dur":5.57,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t4-6.m4a","durJa":7.07,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.28,0.74,1.24,1.34,1.64,2.42,2.92,3.46,3.96,4.26,4.56]}],"bands":{"core1000":71,"core1800":12,"ngsl":6,"tsl":2,"nawl":6,"beyond":3}},"t5":{"sentences":[{"text":"Stanford scientists have engineered a groundbreaking microscope that exposes the intricate machinery of living cells in real time.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-0.m4a","dur":8.78,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-0.m4a","durJa":9.12,"times":[0.0,0.4,1.18,1.6,2.08,2.4,2.94,3.86,4.36,4.8,5.2,5.58,6.34,6.62,6.96,7.4,7.86,8.16]},{"text":"By merging two sophisticated imaging methodologies, the instrument attains remarkable detail without artificial tags.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-1.m4a","dur":7.58,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-1.m4a","durJa":8.84,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.44,0.78,1.38,1.9,3.22,3.34,3.68,4.24,4.9,5.62,6.04,6.72]},{"text":"Conventional approaches frequently depend on markers, which can inadvertently alter cell behavior or degrade over time.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-2.m4a","dur":6.93,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-2.m4a","durJa":9.99,"times":[0.0,0.36,0.9,1.34,1.88,2.2,3.16,3.24,3.42,3.72,4.58,4.9,5.3,5.76,6.08,6.48]},{"text":"The newly designed system circumvents these limitations by utilizing light scattering to capture multiple perspectives.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-3.m4a","dur":7.09,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-3.m4a","durJa":7.54,"times":[0.0,0.08,0.26,0.74,1.24,2.14,2.28,2.68,3.4,3.76,4.3,4.72,5.26,5.54,5.98]},{"text":"Because the technology demands significantly less illumination power, researchers can observe living specimens extensively without inducing harm.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-4.m4a","dur":8.55,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-4.m4a","durJa":9.27,"times":[0.0,0.22,0.42,0.84,1.26,2.04,2.6,3.04,4.06,4.4,4.78,4.96,5.52,6.06,6.8,7.42,8.12]},{"text":"This innovative approach permits simultaneous tracking of numerous cellular components within a natural, unaltered setting.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-5.m4a","dur":7.16,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-5.m4a","durJa":9.01,"times":[0.0,0.18,0.46,1.12,1.5,2.16,2.84,3.16,3.5,4.08,4.5,5.18,5.34,6.1,6.74]},{"text":"Experts anticipate that this complementary tool will unlock new pathways for investigating health, treatments, and biological interactions.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-6.m4a","dur":8.17,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-6.m4a","durJa":10.23,"times":[0.0,0.26,0.76,1.1,1.38,1.74,2.44,2.76,3.12,3.52,3.92,4.34,4.78,5.74,6.48,6.6,6.98]},{"text":"The research team hopes to address previously inaccessible questions about complex biological systems.","voice":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/t5-7.m4a","dur":6.07,"voiceJa":"voice/2026-10-18-health-stanford-scientists-build-new/ja/t5-7.m4a","durJa":7.46,"times":[0.0,0.1,0.38,0.7,0.96,1.18,1.46,2.08,2.7,3.48,3.88,4.24,4.92]}],"bands":{"core1000":53,"core1800":14,"ngsl":10,"tsl":5,"nawl":8,"beyond":10}}},"glossary":[{"word":"researchers","lemma":"researcher","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪˈsɜrtʃərz/","definition":"People who carry out systematic investigations to discover new facts.","tiers":["t2","t3","t4","t5"]},{"word":"technology","lemma":"technology","pos":"noun","ipa":"/tɛkˈnɑlədʒi/","definition":"The application of scientific knowledge for practical purposes.","tiers":["t2","t3","t4","t5"]},{"word":"resolution","lemma":"resolution","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌrɛzəˈluʃən/","definition":"The degree of detail visible in an image or photograph.","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"illumination","lemma":"illumination","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪˌluməˈneɪʃən/","definition":"Lighting or light supplied to something.","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"methodology","lemma":"methodology","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌmɛθəˈdɑlədʒi/","definition":"A system of methods used in a particular area of study.","tiers":["t5"]},{"word":"components","lemm